From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a subagent's approval reaches its parent's
 chat

A background subagent asks for approval under its parent's session key, but the notifier and the prompt belonged to the parent's turn. The turn's end withdrew a prompt the subagent still waited on ("approval was withdrawn before the user answered"), a prompt raised after the turn had nowhere to go, and the viewer's answer was fenced to the turn's execution generation.

A subagent's approval is now bound to the chat. It names the subagent's goal in its description and carries it as subagent, so the card shows which subagent asks. The turn's end keeps the notifier and the waiting subagent prompts while the session has live background subagents, and withdraws only the turn's own prompts. The prompt is registered with the session authority outside the turn's generation, so it stays in the snapshot, answers from any later generation, and keeps an idle chat listed as running for watchers. It waits the same approvals.timeout as a chat prompt.
